window.__finlexFtShardLoaded("intl_tax_0",[[10146,"Overview","Scope & Key Requirements (Public Summary)","Sets out the coordinated 15% global minimum tax framework (Income Inclusion Rule — IIR, Undertaxed Profits Rule — UTPR, and Qualified Domestic Minimum Top-up Tax — QDMTT) for MNE groups with consolidated revenue ≥ EUR 750 million. Directly linked to IAS 12 Pillar Two amendments."],[10146,"GloBE Art. 1–10","15% Global Minimum Tax: Scope, ETR Formula & Charging Order","• Scope (Art. 1.1): MNE groups with consolidated revenue ≥ EUR 750 million in at least 2 of the 4 preceding fiscal years. • Jurisdictional Effective Tax Rate (ETR) (Art. 5.1–5.2): Adjusted Covered Taxes ÷ Net GloBE Income per jurisdiction; if ETR < 15%, Top-up Tax Percentage = 15% − ETR applied to Excess Profit (Net GloBE Income minus Substance-based Income Exclusion for payroll & tangible assets). • Charging rule order: (1) Qualified Domestic Minimum Top-up Tax (QDMTT) collected locally first; (2) Income Inclusion Rule (IIR) at Ultimate Parent Entity; (3) Undertaxed Profits Rule (UTPR) backstop. • Transitional CbCR Safe Harbours & IAS 12 link: temporary safe harbours simplify 2024–2026 compliance; accounting follows IAS 12.4A/88A–88D mandatory deferred tax exception."],[10146,"Official Access","Official Handbook & Reference Entry","Official source (OECD): https://www.oecd.org/en/topics/sub-issues/global-minimum-tax/global-anti-base-erosion-model-rules-pillar-two.html Status: in_force. Detailed paragraph-level summaries and practice notes can be expanded incrementally."],[10147,"Overview","Scope & Key Requirements (Public Summary)","Global template for bilateral double taxation treaties covering residency, permanent establishment (PE), business profits, dividends/interest/royalties withholding tax, and mutual agreement procedures (MAP)."],[10147,"OECD MTC Art. 4–25","Key Treaty Articles: Residency, PE, Passive Income & MAP","• Art. 4 (Resident): tie-breaker rules for dual-resident individuals (permanent home, centre of vital interests) and entities (mutual agreement). • Art. 5 & Art. 7 (Permanent Establishment & Business Profits): source country may tax business profits ONLY if attributable to a PE (fixed place of business, construction site >12 months, or dependent agent). • Arts. 10–12 (Withholding Tax Caps): Dividends (5% substantial holding / 15% portfolio), Interest (10%), Royalties (0% in OECD Model; often 10% in bilateral treaties involving China). • Art. 23 & Art. 25: Elimination of double taxation (exemption or credit method) and Mutual Agreement Procedure (MAP) for cross-border dispute resolution."],[10147,"Official Access","Official Handbook & Reference Entry","Official source (OECD): https://www.oecd.org/en/topics/sub-issues/oecd-model-tax-convention-on-income-and-on-capital.html Status: in_force. Detailed paragraph-level summaries and practice notes can be expanded incrementally."],[10148,"Overview","Scope & Key Requirements (Public Summary)","Authoritative international guidance on the arm's length principle, comparability analysis, transfer pricing methods (CUP, RPM, CPLM, TNMM, Profit Split), intangibles, intra-group services, and Country-by-Country Reporting (CbCR)."],[10148,"OECD TPG Ch. I–X","Arm's Length Principle, Five TP Methods, DEMPE & Documentation","• Arm's Length Principle (Chapter I, MTC Art. 9): controlled transactions between associated enterprises must reflect conditions that independent enterprises would agree to. • Five Transfer Pricing Methods (Chapter II): Traditional Transaction Methods (CUP, Resale Price, Cost Plus) and Transactional Profit Methods (TNMM, Transactional Profit Split). • Intangibles & DEMPE (Chapter VI): profit allocation follows Development, Enhancement, Maintenance, Protection, and Exploitation (DEMPE) functions rather than mere legal ownership. • Three-Tier Documentation (Chapter V / BEPS Action 13): Master File, Local File, and Country-by-Country Report (CbCR for groups ≥ EUR 750m)."],[10148,"Official Access","Official Handbook & Reference Entry","Official source (OECD): https://www.oecd.org/en/topics/sub-issues/transfer-pricing.html Status: in_force. Detailed paragraph-level summaries and practice notes can be expanded incrementally."]]);
